      <workList xml:id="workDesc_f0304a01">
         <work xml:id="work_idde034e17">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_cc102dc5">C4:005</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_id8e46e968" xml:lang="de">Fried. Wilh. Hastfers Goldgrube in Verbesserung der Schaafszucht, nebst einem zuverlässigen Mittel und Rath gegen die Schaafspocken</title>
            <title type="original" xml:id="title_6f4011c4" xml:lang="da">Et Lands Guld-Grube udi Faare-Avelens Forbedring, tilligemed et mod Faare-Kopper tilforladeligt Middel og Raad</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_379e6d77">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_1d8bf22d">Friedrich Wilhelm Hastfer</persName>
               <persName role="translator" xml:id="persName_idc029f258">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_id5a6a87bf">
               <date isodate="1756" xml:id="date_19d913fd">1756</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_idaeceda4b">
               <p xml:id="idm173">While living in Sønderborg, Scheibe produced a series of translations of Danish works. He had already translated <persName xml:id="idm174" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Count Friedrich Wilhelm Hastfer</persName>’s first study on how to keep sheep (1754; SchW C4:001) when Hastfer published his second study dealing with the improvement of sheep-breeding. The book was originally written in Swedish but was soon published in a Danish version, and it is probably this one which Scheibe translated into German.The translation was reviewed in <rend xml:id="idm175" fontstyle="italic">Efterretninger om Nye Bøger og Lærde Sager</rend> in 1756, mentioning that it was an exact translation and more fluent than the Danish version. The present publication was apparently so popular that it received a second edition in 1757, a third in 1762 and finally a fourth in 1767 of which the latter was reviewed in <rend xml:id="idm176" fontstyle="italic">Allgemeine deutsche Bibliothek</rend> (1770). It is possible that the last edition (1767) which was reviewed has received a wrong date of publication in the review (that is, a '2' was misread as a '7'). The editions do not give the name of the translator, but according to Holger Ehrencron-Müller, <rend xml:id="idm177" fontstyle="italic">Bibliotheca Danica</rend> (Copenhagen, 1877–1914) it is Scheibe; he is also mentioned in <rend xml:id="idm178" fontstyle="italic">Efterretninger</rend> (1756).</p>
            </history>
